# A fault of a module goes to its fault endpoint, the root's (roadmap l4.md
# L5, D18): the counter faults once (TEST_COUNTER_FAULT) while the shell
# waits for a key; the root reports it with the module's name, and restarts
# it; the shell goes on.
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER_FAULT
keys: {wait 20}echo hi\n
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>rx286: counter fault #UD at 0007:{c:entry.fault}
echo hi
hi
A:\>
